# Product rules

`spec/prd.md` and `spec/08-product-requirements.md` define **what** finfor delivers; `spec/09`–`13` define **domain rules**; `spec/14`–`18` define implementation-facing product artifacts; specs `00`–`07` define **how**.

## When this applies

- New features, user journeys, API surface, or domain entities
- Scope, persona, or acceptance-criteria changes

## Required actions

1. Read `spec/prd.md` and `spec/08-product-requirements.md` before product-facing work.
2. Read `spec/09-domain-model.md` and `spec/10-deal-state-machine.md` for negotiations, assets, allocation, commissions, NCDA.
3. Read `spec/11-permissions-matrix.md` for roles and confidential fields.
4. Read `spec/13-prospecting-and-partner-ranking.md` for prospecting recommendations or partner scoring.
5. Read `spec/14-ui-routes-copy-and-combos.md` before implementing UI labels, combos, validation messages, or routes.
6. Read `spec/15-api-contract-draft.md` before backend/frontend integration work.
7. Read `spec/16-mvp-backlog-and-acceptance.md` for MVP story acceptance.
8. Update the relevant spec when scope, journeys, or domain rules change (same PR or spec-first PR).
9. Map screens to `spec/03-page-layout-guidelines.md` patterns.
10. Tie discovery checklist items in `spec/README.md` to filled sections in `08`.
11. Keep UI labels/copy in Portuguese; keep code identifiers and comments in English.

Do not implement product behavior that contradicts an agreed product/domain spec without updating the spec first.
